---
title: "Introduction to Diesel Engine"
code: "DSL-111"
category: "diesel"
credits: "2"
prerequisites: []
corequisites: []
---

Studies the modern diesel engine, including its fuel, cooling, induction, and exhaust systems. Covers construction, fabrication, maintenance, tune-up, and minor repair and adjustment. Lecture 1 hour. Laboratory 2 hours. Total 3 hours per week. Additional course fee applies.
